OpenAL Soft 1.25.2: build fix for targets where int32_t is not `int`.

Applied by scripts/3ds/build-openal.sh (patch -p1, from the source root).

Problem: common/altypes.hpp maps the fixed-width types to its "strict"
number wrappers via explicit specializations of al::make_strict<> for
std::int8_t ... std::uint64_t, then defines

    using sys_int  = al::make_strict_t<int>;
    using sys_uint = al::make_strict_t<unsigned>;

On arm-none-eabi (devkitARM, newlib) GCC defines __INT32_TYPE__ as
`long int`, so std::int32_t is `long` and there is no specialization for
plain `int`/`unsigned`. Every TU then fails with

    common/altypes.hpp:114:7: error: no type named 'type' in 'struct al::make_strict<int>'
    common/altypes.hpp:508:39: error: 'sys_uint' does not name a type

Fix: add constrained partial specializations that map `int`/`unsigned` to
i32/u32 only when they are distinct from int32_t/uint32_t and the same size.
On targets where int32_t is int (all upstream-supported ones) the
constraints are false and nothing changes. Not fixed upstream as of
master on 2026-10-10.

--- a/common/altypes.hpp
+++ b/common/altypes.hpp
@@ -109,6 +109,14 @@
 template<> struct make_strict<std::uint64_t> { using type = u64; };
 template<> struct make_strict<float> { using type = f32; };
 template<> struct make_strict<double> { using type = f64; };
+/* Targets where int32_t is not int (e.g. arm-none-eabi/newlib, where it is
+ * long): map the plain int types to the 32-bit strict types as well. */
+template<typename T> requires(std::same_as<T, int> && !std::same_as<int, std::int32_t>
+    && sizeof(int) == sizeof(std::int32_t))
+struct make_strict<T> { using type = i32; };
+template<typename T> requires(std::same_as<T, unsigned> && !std::same_as<unsigned, std::uint32_t>
+    && sizeof(unsigned) == sizeof(std::uint32_t))
+struct make_strict<T> { using type = u32; };
 
 template<typename T>
 using make_strict_t = typename make_strict<T>::type;
